name: emitter-honesty
kind: inferred
shape: categorical
face: in
membrane: false
note: the emitted text does not mean what the source spelled — the
  compiler produced output the backend either refuses or would read
  differently. Fires when a lowering door stops passing source bytes
  through verbatim and starts respelling them (e.g. `&&`/`||` -> Zig's
  `and`/`or`), closing the gap between "accepted surface" and "compiles
  to the same thing". Cousin of toolchain-soundness: that one is
  compile-clean-then-misbehaves; this one is source-valid-then-emit-lies.
